# Build, test and lint artefacts — one root, one `rm -rf`. Turborepo's cache
# obeys it through `cacheDir` in turbo.json; the per-task log it drops beside
# every package does not — the path `<package>/.turbo/turbo-<task>.log` is not
# configurable, and an unignored one feeds its own hash back into the next run,
# so a second `turbo run` never hits the cache.
.artifacts/
**/.turbo/

# Dependencies
node_modules/

# OS junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editor junk
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# Local state a run leaves on this checkout — never a build's output:
# Claude Code's harness folder, spwn's own runtime state, the chief-mode
# test agent dir, and the project an e2e run scaffolds when it is given
# `specs/` as its cwd. Every one is anchored to the repository root:
# unanchored, `.claude/` and `.spwn/` also swallowed the committed golden
# fixtures under packages/runtimes/testdata/ and specs/, and four
# `!` lines had to rescue them.
/.claude/
/.spwn/
/spwn/agents/
/specs/spwn/
/specs/spwn.yaml

# Archives (agent exports etc.)
*.tar.gz
*.tar
*.bak

# Mirror of /catalog/ generated by `go:generate` into the Go package
# tree so //go:embed can reach it (embed can't use .. or cross-module
# paths). Source of truth is /catalog/ at the repo root; refresh via
# `make generate` (or `go generate ./packages/dependency/...`).
# Makefile wires `generate` as a prerequisite for both `build` and
# `test`, so any make-driven workflow sees it. Fresh `go build`
# without Make needs one `go generate` first.
/packages/dependency/internal/adapters/spwn/content/
